      "description": "is_palindrome() cleans the input (`s.lower().replace(\" \", \"\")`) but then compares the original `s` against `s[::-1]` instead of comparing the cleaned string against its reverse. This causes palindromes with uppercase letters or spaces to be incorrectly rejected, contradicting the docstring. Fix: `cleaned = s.lower().replace(\" \", \"\"); return cleaned == cleaned[::-1]`.",
